# Build context for backend/Dockerfile (context = repo root, for fly deploy and
# docker-compose alike). The image needs backend/ (package + pyproject.toml)
# and db/migrations/ (alembic.ini + versions, for the release command). Nothing
# below is either of those.

# Secrets. Settings reads ./.env at runtime (env_file=".env", WORKDIR /app), so
# a baked file fills in any variable Fly does not set, and ships the key in an
# image layer. Configuration belongs in Fly secrets and fly.toml [env].
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# VCS, worktrees, local database backups, editor/agent state
.git
.worktrees
backups
**/.claude
**/.DS_Store

# Frontend build output and dependencies (deployed separately, on Vercel)
**/node_modules
frontend/.next

# Python caches and local virtualenvs
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.venv

# Local logs
**/*.log
**/logs
